  "description": "The wire contract for HoloDb clients and servers: length-prefixed TCP framing plus a columnar-preserving binary codec that encodes requests and decodes responses as typed column arrays (long[], double[], string[]) instead of JSON. Includes protocol version negotiation and three exception types for version skew, malformed frames, and server errors. Use this if you are implementing a HoloDb server or building a custom client; most applications should use EvaluatedApplications.HoloDb.Client instead.",
